Greengram reads gramsrv as a reference and writes its own code. Any file
copied from it keeps its original copyright line and carries a
"changed by Greengram" note describing the changes. Those files stay under
Apache-2.0; the combined work is distributed under AGPL-3.0.

Copied files:
- internal/botapi/formatted_text.go, from internal/botapi/formatted_text.go:
  Bot API parse_mode (HTML, Markdown, MarkdownV2) parsing. gramsrv's domain
  entity types swapped for local ones.

Copied data:
- internal/api/peercolors.json, from internal/seed/appearance/
  default_appearance_seed.json (peer_colors, peer_profile_colors): Telegram's
  name and profile color palettes. Changed by Greengram: trimmed to the
  fields help.getPeerColors needs.
- internal/api/timezones.json, from internal/seed/catalog/timezones.json:
  Telegram's help.getTimezonesList answer (zone ids, names, UTC offsets).
  Unchanged.

The language packs langpack.* serves are not in this repository. They are
Telegram's translations as gramsrv redistributes them (data/langpack, commit
0dcf3eb); scripts/langpacks.py builds the directory from a gramsrv checkout,
see docs/languages.md.
